      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.69,
            0.049,
            0.86,
            0.065
          ],
          "content": "Fractions in Disguise"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.089,
            0.592,
            0.226
          ],
          "content": "7. What is 5% of 40? What is 40% of 5? What is 25% of 12? What is 12% of 25? What is 15% of 60? What is 60% of 15? What do you notice? Can you make a general statement and justify it using algebra, comparing x% of y and y% of x?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.229,
            0.593,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": "8. A school is organising an excursion for its students. 40% of them are Grade 8 students and the rest are Grade 9"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.606,
            0.082,
            0.848,
            0.269
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_28_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.284,
            0.845,
            0.324
          ],
          "content": "students. Among these Grade 8 students, 60% are girls. [**Hint:** Drawing a rough diagram can help]."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.331,
            0.847,
            0.37
          ],
          "content": "(i) What percentage of the students going to the excursion are Grade 8 girls?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.374,
            0.844,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": "(ii) If the total number of students going to the excursion is 160, how many of them are Grade 8 girls?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.416,
            0.811,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": "9. A shopkeeper sells pencils at a price such that the selling price of 3 pencils is equal to the cost of 5 pencils. Does he make a profit or a loss? What is his profit or loss percentage?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.825,
            0.413,
            0.926,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_28_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.482,
            0.846,
            0.522
          ],
          "content": "10. The bus fares were increased by 3% last year and by 4% this year. What is the overall percentage price increase in the last 2 years?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.53,
            0.847,
            0.588
          ],
          "content": "11. If the length of a rectangle is increased by 10% and the area is unchanged, by what percentage (exactly) does the breadth decrease by?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.597,
            0.644,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": "12. The percentage of ingredients in a 65 g chips packet is shown in the picture. Find out the weight each ingredient makes up in this packet."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.681,
            0.643,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": "13. Three shops sell the same items at the same price. The shops offer deals as follows: Shop A: “Buy 1 and get 1 free” Shop B: “Buy 2 and get 1 free” Shop C: “Buy 3 and get 1 free”"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.671,
            0.604,
            0.874,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_28_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.785,
            0.422,
            0.805
          ],
          "content": "Answer the following:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.809,
            0.847,
            0.848
          ],
          "content": "(i) If the price of one item is ₹100, what is the effective price per item in each shop? Arrange the shops from cheapest to costliest."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.851,
            0.845,
            0.89
          ],
          "content": "(ii) For each shop, calculate the percentage discount on the items. [**Hint:** Compare the free items to the total items you receive.]"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.893,
            0.847,
            0.915
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Suppose you need 4 items. Which shop would you choose? Why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.876,
